---
title: Partners
sidebar:
  order: 12
---

Each partner has a world file in `world/partner/`, such as `world/partner/kooper.c`, and a battle file in `battle/partner/`, such as `battle/partner/kooper.c`.

## How a partner's field ability works

A world file ends with `OVL_DEF_PARTNER()`, which lists what the partner does in the world:

| Field | What it is |
| --- | --- |
| `init` | A C function that runs when the partner appears, and sets it up, such as its collision size. |
| `takeOut` | The EVT script that runs while the partner comes out. |
| `update` | The EVT script that runs while the partner follows the player. |
| `useAbility` | The EVT script that runs when the player presses **C-Down**. When it ends, `update` starts again. |
| `putAway` | The EVT script that runs while the partner goes away, such as when the player switches partners. |
| `canUseAbility` | A C function that returns whether the player can use the ability. Without one, the player always can. |
| `canPlayerOpenMenus` | A C function that returns whether the player can open menus, such as while the ability is in use. |
| `isFlying` | Whether the partner flies. |
| `idle` | The partner's idle animation. |

Some partners also set `testFirstStrike`, `preBattle`, `postBattle`, `onEnterMap`, or `syncPlayerPosition` for what they do around battles and map changes.

Each of these EVT scripts calls [API functions](/papermario-dx/evt-scripts/call-c/) that do the work in C over several frames. For most partners, the field ability is in an API function called `UseAbility`, such as in `world/partner/kooper.c`.

## How a partner's battle moves work

A battle file defines the partner like an [actor](/papermario-dx/battles/actors/), with a blueprint, parts, and tables. On the partner's turn, its `EVS_ExecuteAction` gets the move the player chose with `GetMenuSelection`, and runs that move's EVT script:

```c
Switch(LVar2)
    CaseEq(MOVE_HEADBONK1)
        ExecWait(EVS_Attack_Headbonk1)
    CaseEq(MOVE_TATTLE)
        ExecWait(EVS_Move_Tattle)
    // ...
EndSwitch
```

Each partner has six moves in `registry/moves.yaml`, in this order:

| Position | Offered | Goombario's |
| --- | --- | --- |
| 1 | At normal rank | Headbonk (`Headbonk1`) |
| 2 | At Super rank | Headbonk (`Headbonk2`) |
| 3 | At Ultra rank | Headbonk (`Headbonk3`) |
| 4 | Always | Tattle |
| 5 | From Super rank | Charge |
| 6 | From Ultra rank | Multibonk |

The battle menu finds a partner's moves by their position, so you can change a partner's moves but not add more. A move's entry sets its name, FP cost, and targets, and its EVT script deals damage with `PartnerDamageEnemy`. See [Moves](/papermario-dx/battles/moves/) for what the fields and arguments mean.

## Changing a partner's move

This example makes Goombario's normal-rank Headbonk deal 2 damage per hit instead of 1.

{% steps %}
1. Open `battle/partner/goombario.c`, and find `EVS_Attack_Headbonk1`.
2. Before each `PartnerDamageEnemy` in it, change `Add(LVar0, 1)` to `Add(LVar0, 2)`. There are three: two for the first hit, and one for the second.

   ```c
   Call(GetChargeAmount)
   Add(LVar0, 2)
   Call(PartnerDamageEnemy, LVar0, DAMAGE_TYPE_JUMP, 0, 0, LVar0, BS_FLAGS1_NICE_HIT | BS_FLAGS1_INCLUDE_POWER_UPS)
   ```

   `LVar0` starts as the damage that Charge added, and `Add` puts the base damage on top.
{% /steps %}

To change a move's FP cost, change its `costFP` in `registry/moves.yaml`. For example, to make Power Shell cost 2 FP, set `costFP: 2` in the `PowerShell` entry.

To test a change, open the [debug menu](/papermario-dx/debug/debug-menu/), use **Edit Partners** to add the partner at the rank you changed, then start a battle with **Battle Select**.

## Giving the player a partner

In a map, `ChangeNpcToPartner` turns one of the map's NPCs into a partner, adds the partner to the party, and makes it the active partner. Include it in the map's file, then call it with the NPC and the partner:

```c
#include "world/common/util/ChangeNpcToPartner.inc.c"

EvtScript EVS_KooperJoins = {
    // ...
    Call(ChangeNpcToPartner, NPC_Kooper, PARTNER_KOOPER)
    Return
    End
};
```
